# The Influence of Subject, Publisher Type, and Quantity Published on Journal Prices.

**Authors:** Moline, Sandra R.

## Abstract
Compares mean 1985 subscription prices and mean cents per thousand characters of scholarly journals in the humanities, social sciences, and sciences. Similar comparisons are made for journals published by associations, scholarly organizations, and commercial publishers, and the data from this study are compared with data from a study using 1973 prices. (17 references) (Author/CLB)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ390966

